<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Siegebreaker (VFEP v3.09,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are Siegebreaker's,
    VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets research prereq included. Docs/Specs/Set-Tuning.md is the tuning's
    design record, Docs/Research/VFEP_WARCASKET_STATS.md tabulates the sets it is priced against.

    Tuning. Reference numbers are VFEP's 10th-generation sets (Siegebreaker, Guardian,
    Controller, Sarcophagus, Brute). A squad-support suit on the tier's shared chassis, its
    budget spent on the medic kit and its fills rather than on the pilot's own protection:
    - Sharp 2 / Blunt 1 / Heat 1 on all three pieces, the tier's shared values. Blunt 1.5 is
      Guardian's and Brute's, paid for in plasteel; this set has no claim to it.
    - EnergyShieldEnergyMax 1.5 at EnergyShieldRechargeRate 0.01, the tier's baseline
      (Guardian, Controller, Sarcophagus); Siegebreaker's 2.5 and Brute's 5.0 are their
      specialties. The bubble blocks ranged fire only, what a medic needs to reach a patient
      under fire.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 6 / Plasteel 145 / Uranium 50 / MedicineUltratech 10. The
      components are VFEP's tech-complexity dial (the utility sets 6, Controller 12, Brute 4),
      the plasteel the utility sets' 145 to 150. The medicine is the suite's full first fill:
      vanilla prices a pack's whole fill, VFEP none (Aerial, Shock), and Sarcophagus already
      demands ten glitterworld kits per set for flavour alone, so the suite ships full and
      paid. At market value (plasteel 9, component 200, uranium 6, glitterworld medicine 50)
      the full set is 5621 silver, 5085 before the fills: Siegebreaker 4195, Sarcophagus 4785,
      Guardian 5164, Brute 5220, Controller about 6330. Parts are untradeable and destroyed on
      drop, so market value is colony wealth and raid points only. The shoulders and helmet
      scale at the 10th-gen piece ratios; see their headers.

    apparel tags: WarcasketVeteran (VFEP's 10th-gen tag) puts the set on the veteran raid
    pawnkinds of both VFEP factions and Odyssey's VFEP_Salvager_Warcasket; WarcasketAll is
    VFEP_General. Threat and flavor only: AI pawns never cast apparel abilities, so a raider
    in the set is a Siegebreaker with the baseline shield.

    Mechanite dressing: VEF CompAbilitiesApparel grants MDWC_MechaniteDressing (AbilityDefs/
    MechaniteDressing.xml), fed by the medicine suite beside it. The ability reads the suite off
    the apparel that grants it, so both comps must sit on this one def. The suite is
    MedicWarcasket.CompProperties_DressingSuite (Source/1.6/Comps/), a CompApparelReloadable
    whose props class sets the compClass, so none is declared here; its DefInjected keys read
    comps.CompDressingSuite, since the handle is the comp class. It holds kits of ONE medicine,
    ammoDef: one kit is one medicine item (ammoCountPerCharge 1) and one vanilla charge, and
    maxCharges 10 is the kits held when full. Each kit treats severityPerKit (20) severity, one
    vanilla treatment's cap. chargeNoun "kit": the stats pane and the reload text count the
    suite in kits. The free first fill (vanilla's full charge on creation) is ten kits of
    ammoDef, the costList's MedicineUltratech 10. ammoDef and maxCharges are mod
    settings defaulting to these values. baseReloadTicks 60 and Standard_Reload are the
    family's reloadable defaults. displayGizmoWhileUndrafted true alongside the ability's
    showUndrafted: a medic dresses wounds in the hospital too.

    Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/, laid out as VFEP's sets are. The
    worn graphic is Graphic_Multi (the _north/_east/_south facings); the item icon is the
    parent's Graphic_Single, read from the bare-named file, which is a copy of the _south facing.

    Masked tint, all three pieces (VFEP's sets have no masks; vanilla's prestige armors are
    the pattern): CutoutComplex on both graphics of each piece, worn via apparel.useWornGraphicMask, so the
    CompColorable colour paints the mask's red areas and the black-masked medical cross and
    shoulder trim keep their painted colour (apparel graphics pass white as colorTwo). Mask
    names differ by graphic class: Graphic_Multi reads <path>_northm, Graphic_Single <path>_m.

    Own trait on equip: traitsOnEquip grants MDWC_WarcasketTrait_Medic (TraitDefs/
    WarcasketTrait_Medic.xml), not VFEP_WarcasketTrait, because the Medic's work profile must
    differ from VFEP's (Doctor open) and a child ApparelExtension can only add to what a granted
    trait blocks, never subtract; the trait is mirrored from VFEP's at startup so the patch mods
    that reshape VFEP's profile reshape ours. traitsOnUnequip keeps VFEP_Shellcasket, the shared
    "cut out of a warcasket" state every add-on set uses, so removal surgery and re-entombing in
    any warcasket behave as for VFEP's own sets.

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicate
    extensions in a Def.ResolveReferences prefix, highest priority surviving, and
    ApparelExtension.Merge does not copy every field; at equal priority the parent's copy
    would win. At priority 1 every field of ours, from any load root, is kept. Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat patches reach this def from 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml (EVA tag, cold insulation),
    1.6/Mods/VanillaGravshipExpanded/Patches/VacuumResistance.xml and the
    1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root (plating on CE's scale, bulk, carry capacity,
    shield, costs); see their headers.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>MDWC_Warcasket_Medic</defName>
    <label>medic warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with standard protection, fitted with a mechanite dressing suite that breaks loaded medicine down into carrier mechanites and streams them onto a patient's wounds.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket shell with standard protection, fitted with a mechanite dressing suite that breaks loaded medicine down into carrier mechanites and streams them onto a patient's wounds.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Medic was its rig for the surgeons who had served beside them.\n\nThe shell's dressing suite tends a squadmate's wounds where they fall, the pauldrons' injector keeps them on their feet for a few hours more, and the helmet's visor diagnoses what no bandage treats. Plating and shield are the generation's standard, so a Medic fights a step behind the line, and a squad that fields one holds out long after its bandages would have run out.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedic</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>50</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>80</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>80</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
      <EnergyShieldRechargeRate>0.01</EnergyShieldRechargeRate>
      <EnergyShieldEnergyMax>1.5</EnergyShieldEnergyMax>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <PsychicSensitivity>-0.5</PsychicSensitivity>
      <ToxicResistance>0.5</ToxicResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>6</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>145</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
      <MedicineUltratech>10</MedicineUltratech>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketMedic/WarcasketMedic</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="MedicWarcasket.CompProperties_DressingSuite">
        <maxCharges>10</maxCharges>
        <ammoDef>MedicineUltratech</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <chargeNoun>kit</chargeNoun>
        <severityPerKit>20</severityPerKit>
        <displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>true</displayGizmoWhileUndrafted>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>MDWC_MechaniteDressing</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.CompProperties_ShieldBubble">
        <compClass>VEF.Apparels.CompShieldBubble</compClass>
        <blockRangedAttack>true</blockRangedAttack>
        <blockMeleeAttack>false</blockMeleeAttack>
        <showWhenDrafted>true</showWhenDrafted>
        <showOnHostiles>true</showOnHostiles>
        <showOnNeutralInCombat>true</showOnNeutralInCombat>
        <shieldTexPath>Other/ShieldBubble</shieldTexPath>
        <chargeFullyWhenMade>true</chargeFullyWhenMade>
        <minShieldSize>2.1</minShieldSize>
        <maxShieldSize>2.7</maxShieldSize>
        <disableRotation>true</disableRotation>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>MDWC_WarcasketTrait_Medic</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
